module lib/hf/rhf
  Restricted Hartree-Fock (RHF), checked against PySCF 2.5.0.

  For a closed shell, with as many alpha as beta electrons, RHF puts both
  spins in the same orbitals: one total density, `F = H + J - K/2`, two
  electrons in each occupied orbital. The loop that solves it is
  lib/hf/scf_loop's, shared with UHF and ROHF, so this module holds no loop
  of its own. It holds the RHF checks: every combination of the registries'
  members on water, other molecules and basis sets, a basis with a nearly
  dependent vector, a geometry with two RHF states, import of PySCF's
  densities, and a run far past convergence. The helpers below build the
  setups those checks run from the reference integrals of lib/hfref.

rhf_t_all_presets  @df3bde8a
  how   Run every preset of `rhf_t_presets` on water 6-31G and keep the worst
        gap of each kind: energy and density against PySCF, the second energy
        formula, the commutator, the electron count and idempotency, then
        count how many converged, in an `RhfPresets` record.

rhf_t_import  @8e41b463
  how   For one stretched-water density: take the plain step from it and
        compare the density and the energy it gives; converge further with
        tighter tolerances and see whether the density moves; take the plain
        step again from there. The five measurements come back as an
        `RhfImport` record.
  why   Stretched water has two RHF states. A step that moves PySCF's density
        by as little as PySCF's own step does shows the Fock build and the
        filling rule agree with PySCF's at that state
        [test "the fixed-point step from each imported stretched-water density matches PySCF's own step"].
